        "~/wave/context/B.md": {
          "content": "# Wave package B\n\nWORKING TREE: the isolated worktree you are started in (your cwd). Do every read, edit, test and command inside it; never touch files outside it.\n\nYou own only these paths (files_owned); change nothing else:\n- b.txt\n\nCarry-over: anything you need changed outside files_owned goes, one self-contained instruction per line with file paths, into <HOME>/wave/carry/B.carry.md -- never into the code. Finish your own scope anyway.\n\nRead the current code before trusting the spec's paths: other packages have moved code since it was written.\n\nDo NOT commit, stash, reset or checkout. To set changes aside use `agent-exec shelf push` / `agent-exec shelf pop`, never `git stash`.\n\nIf the task cannot be done as specified, reply with a first line `ESCALATE: <reason>` and change nothing further.\n\nNetwork access goes through an allowlist. A blocked request (proxy 403, \"blocked by network allowlist\", connection refused to an external host) must not be worked around: no other mirrors, no proxy or environment changes, no hand-vendoring. If the task cannot be finished without it, reply with a first line `ESCALATE: network <host>[, <host>...]`.\n\nDo not commit: leave every change uncommitted in the working tree.\n",
          "shape": "text"
        },
